  "headline": "Indonesian Coalition Parties Defer Vice President Selection Choice",
  "seoTitle": "Indonesia Coalition Defers VP Selection",
  "metaDescription": "Indonesian political parties supporting the administration have agreed to allow President Prabowo to decide on a new vice president successor.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "President Prabowo is tasked with selecting a new vice president following the upcoming vacancy.",
    "Major political parties in the coalition have generally declined to nominate internal candidates for the position.",
    "Internal and external discussions are ongoing, with some factions proposing specific names while others prefer a consultative process."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The political landscape in Indonesia is currently focused on the search for a new vice president to succeed Gibran. President Prabowo Subianto has indicated that he will finalize his decision regarding the successor upon returning from his official visits to Manila and Shenzhen. The coalition of political parties supporting the administration has reached a general consensus to leave the final selection entirely to the President. While some organizations affiliated with the Gerindra Party have suggested individuals such as Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, several major coalition partners have stated they are not putting forward their own members for the role. Other parties have emphasized the importance of choosing a figure with extensive experience working alongside the President. Discussions remain active as stakeholders evaluate potential candidates and the process for formalizing the new appointment.",
